# ==========================================================
# Cell 16 : LINKING + TRAVERSAL  (SPARQL, no LLM)
#
#   ITERATED, NOT A PROPERTY PATH: SPARQL property paths require fixed
#   predicate IRIs -- variables are illegal inside a path -- and the
#   {n,m} cardinality forms were removed from SPARQL 1.1 before it was
#   finalised. With distinct predicates per relationship, the options
#   are a chained-statement query or an iterated 1-hop query. Iterating
#   wins: rdflib evaluates a chained double-statement pattern as a
#   near-cartesian join, and each hop multiplies it again.
#
#   OUTGOING ONLY (Wikipedia-style): hop 1 = the seed's own outgoing
#   hyperlinks, hop 2 = those targets' own outgoing hyperlinks, and so
#   on -- pure forward expansion, never looking backward at who links
#   TO a node.
#
#   CONSEQUENCE OF THIS: Cell 10 only ever writes document -> entity
#   edges (a document is always rdf:subject, never rdf:object). Under
#   outgoing-only traversal, a seed that resolves to a pure ENTITY node
#   (something documents link to, but which itself links to nothing)
#   has zero outgoing edges and yields nothing at hop 1. That is
#   expected under this model, not a bug -- a DOCUMENT seed is what
#   drives expansion, the same way a Wikipedia article's own hyperlinks
#   are what you follow outward from it.
# ==========================================================
